{{~##
 One constant set's declarations.

 C has nothing to nest a set in, so each constant carries its set's name and they end up
 flat - but they still get a file per set, because that is the unit the sheets add and
 remove.

 A value the preprocessor can hold is a `#define`. One that cannot - a uuid, which is a
 struct - is declared `extern const` here and defined once in the matching source file,
 because a struct defined in a header would be a separate object in every translation unit
 that included it.
##~}}
{{ include 'c-header-head.sbn' ~}}
/* Generated from {{ set.location }}
{{~ for line in set.comment ~}}
 *
 * {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
 */
{{~ for constant in set.constants ~}}
{{~ for line in constant.comment ~}}
/* {{ line }} */
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if constant.is_extern ~}}
extern const {{ constant.type }} {{ constant.name }};
{{~ else ~}}
#define {{ constant.name }} {{ constant.value }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'c-header-foot.sbn' ~}}
